 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "It may be that purer minds now behold\nThe soul of this fair moon; but again\nAwe wearily when it is ago\nAnd the watch to-day is broken,\nAnd a shade of midnight shadows shadows\nThe silence and dimness, and,\nNor do I know how, that little moon\nOf all our light and all our light,\nTo take from darkness a shadow now,\nFor a shadow's sake on earth. Nay never\nThou tellest us thy path again.\nYet if it was thou alone",
